[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717647829","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3717647829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3717647829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dls3V","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T07:27:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T07:52:51Z","body":"Last night I finally found out how to use the magnetometer and what its values actually mean. I was very confused that it didn't point directly to the north for me, but instead it showed me some vertical line pointing down slightly tilted towards the north. Turns out, in the northern hemisphere (not just on the north pole), the Earth's magnetic field points into the Earth/into the ground, not just to the north. It was interesting to find out.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717647829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756307822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3756307822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3756307822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7f5LVu","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T18:33:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T18:33:15Z","body":"Thank you for your review, Alex2782! I will think of a better description and thanks, I will take a look at the demo later when I can!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3756307822/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3763093823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3763093823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3763093823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gTEE_","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T11:12:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T11:28:22Z","body":"Hi, I just tried the sensors demo and here is the orientation of the cubes I have and the phone's orientation that was used:\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Cubes' orientation</summary>\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_2026-01-17-16-07-15-397_org godotengine editor v4 debug](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d4714dc5-39e5-434d-ad10-8cadb7f777e5)\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Phone's orientation</summary>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"960\" height=\"1280\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11fe5d95-d464-4639-a1f3-dd6946d559e8\" />\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nMay I ask how different were the cubes' orientations between your phone and your tablet, Alex2782?\r\n\r\n> I'm not sure if `held in front of you` is the correct description for Android devices. Unfortunately, I can't say what the correct answer is either. More research and testing are needed.\r\n\r\nWhat about \"For a device held in front of you with the screen side pointed towards you\"?\r\n\r\nAnd I also should specify where the \"up\" is depending on the phone's orientation (portrait or landscape)\r\n\"Note that the up vector (up direction) always points to the upper side of the phone's screen that is natural to the current orientation (portrait or landscape).\" if that makes sense","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3763093823/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3781140436","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3781140436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3781140436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hX5_U","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T21:00:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T21:21:42Z","body":"> May I ask how different were the cubes' orientations between your phone and your tablet, Alex2782?\r\n\r\nHere I placed my smartphone on top of my tablet, and only then did I start the app on both devices.\r\nMy tablet has a case with a stand, maybe a 20° tilt.\r\n\r\n![PXL_20260121_174903692 MP](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/409fa10c-a8b3-4025-b7c4-b7fbbbdd321f)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3781140436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3782571308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3782571308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3782571308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hdXUs","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T05:31:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T10:39:26Z","body":"Hm, does the phone also show this orientation if it's away from the tablet or anything else metallic/magnetic?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3782571308/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786334040","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786334040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786334040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hrt9Y","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T19:38:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T19:38:46Z","body":"> Hm, does the phone also show this orientation if it's away from the tablet or anything else metallic/magnetic?\r\n\r\nThanks for the tip, I think it's because of the tablet case, it has magnets in it 😄 \r\n\r\n<details><summary>portrait orientation</summary>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1080\" height=\"2340\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260122_193538\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a418341-6f37-48d1-8ebc-ccc62686133f\" />\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n<details><summary>landscape orientation</summary>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2340\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Screenshot_20260122_193628\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54b4ef75-3130-4a64-8212-9568222fb5d6\" />\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n---------------------------\r\n\r\n### get_accelerometer\r\n\r\n```\r\nReturns the acceleration, including the force of gravity, in m/s² of the device's accelerometer sensor, if the device has one. Otherwise, the method returns [constant Vector3.ZERO]. See also [method get_gravity].\r\nFor a device held in front of you, the returned axes are defined as follows:\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t+X ... -X: left ... right;\r\n\t\t\t\t+Y ... -Y: bottom ... top;\r\n\t\t\t\t+Z ... -Z: farther ... closer.\r\n\r\nThe gravity part value is measured as a vector with length of about [code]9.8[/code] away from the center of the Earth, which is a negative Y value.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nI verified these values ​​in the demo using my smartphone.\r\n\r\nI don't understand `+Z ... -Z: farther ... closer.` \r\n\r\n- On my smartphone, `Z = 0` when I hold it upright. \r\n- If I lay my smartphone on the table with the display facing up, then I see `Z = -9.8`. \r\n- If I turn my smartphone over with the display facing down, `Z = 9.8`. \r\n\r\nSo it's a tilt and has nothing to do with \"farther\" and \"closer,\" right? It doesn't matter whether it's landscape or portrait mode.\r\n\r\n------------------\r\n\r\n- `Y = 0` Portrait orientation\r\n- `Y = -9.8` Landscape orientation (rotated to the left)\r\n- `Y = 9.8` Landscape orientation (rotated to the right)\r\n\r\n\r\n------------------\r\n\r\n- `X = 9.8` Portrait orientation \r\n- `X = -9.8`  Portrait orientation, rotated 180°\r\n- `X = 0` Landscape orientation\r\n\r\n---------------------\r\n\r\nPerhaps we should refer more to the Android documentation (we use SensorManager).\r\nhttps://developer.android.com/develop/sensors-and-location/sensors/sensors_overview#sensors-coords\r\n\r\nThe documentation mentions the `default orientation`, which sounds like it should differ between tablets and smartphones, but when I compare the X/Y-values ​​with the screenshots from my tablet, I think they are identical in landscape mode.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786334040/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786379116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786379116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786379116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hr49s","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T19:51:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T19:51:26Z","body":"Thank you for your notes!\nHm, I think an explanation for farther/closer would be something like this:\nLet's say your phone is laying on a table with its screen facing up and you're looking at your phone from above. The Z value is -9.8.\nNow, if you were to quickly move your phone *closer* to you, the Z value will get even lower (so it goes even more into the *negative* area).\nIf you pick up your phone while still holding it with the screen facing up and move it *farther* from you, the value will start to rise (maybe it can even become *positive* with enough force).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786379116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786411798","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786411798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786411798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hsA8W","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T19:58:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T19:58:31Z","body":"> ------------------\n> \n> - `Y = 0` Portrait orientation\n> - `Y = -9.8` Landscape orientation (rotated to the left)\n> - `Y = 9.8` Landscape orientation (rotated to the right)\n> \n> \n> ------------------\n> \n> - `X = 9.8` Portrait orientation \n> - `X = -9.8`  Portrait orientation, rotated 180°\n> - `X = 0` Landscape orientation\n> \n> ---------------------\n\nI feel like it's only true if Android doesn't change the orientation of the screen 😅\nFrom my testing, if I remember correctly, at some point the Y value was -9.8, and when I turned my phone upside down quickly it became 9.8, and after the screen adjusted to the new orientation the value became negative again.\nI will also need to check the values if the game is in portrait mode, not just landscape.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786411798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786417515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786417515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786417515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hsCVr","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T19:59:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T19:59:32Z","body":"> Hm, I think an explanation for farther/closer would be something like this:\r\n> Let's say your phone is laying on a table with its screen facing up and you're looking at your phone from above. The Z value is -9.8.\r\n> Now, if you were to quickly move your phone _closer_ to you, the Z value will get even lower (so it goes even more into the _negative_ area).\r\n\r\nI tried it out: `Z = -9.8` when I'm doing nothing, but as soon as I move quickly towards or away from me, the value `Z = -11`. So it doesn't get greater than `-9.8` (+Z = further, I couldn't reproduce it).\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786417515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786440808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786440808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786440808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hsIBo","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T20:03:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T20:03:52Z","body":"> I feel like it's only true if Android doesn't change the orientation of the screen 😅\r\n\r\nOh, you're right, the app has a fixed orientation, that could be the reason.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786440808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786518238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3786518238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3786518238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hsa7e","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T20:20:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T21:33:23Z","body":"> > Hm, I think an explanation for farther/closer would be something like this:\r\n> > Let's say your phone is laying on a table with its screen facing up and you're looking at your phone from above. The Z value is -9.8.\r\n> > Now, if you were to quickly move your phone _closer_ to you, the Z value will get even lower (so it goes even more into the _negative_ area).\r\n> \r\n> I tried it out: `Z = -9.8` when I'm doing nothing, but as soon as I move quickly towards or away from me, the value `Z = -11`. So it doesn't get greater than `-9.8` (+Z = further, I couldn't reproduce it).\r\n\r\nThat's strange, because I can reproduce it if I quickly move my phone away from me and closer to the ground:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cdfc815-ee8a-49f6-9f5f-810fdba366a4\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3786518238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3787053241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3787053241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3787053241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hudi5","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T22:25:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T22:29:49Z","body":"It's hard to say; I very quickly picked up my smartphone with both hands and put it back down on the table. But I can't hold my smartphone straight while doing that. Sometimes I also saw `Z = -5` when I put my smartphone back down on the table.\r\n\r\n- `the acceleration, including the force of gravity, in m/s² `\r\n- `+Z ... -Z: farther ... closer.`\r\n\r\nI think I understand that now, although the results aren't always clear-cut. My downward movement adds more acceleration to the gravitational force (acceleration), causing the constant -9.8 to be exceeded, as if the Earth had a stronger gravitational pull. (sometimes `Z = -18` in my video)\r\n\r\nHow can we document this in a way that's easy to understand for everyone who knows even less about physics than I do? 😃 \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5a5566a0-a3f9-4313-afb5-ceccd4f1a46f\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3787053241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788218164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3788218164","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3788218164,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hy580","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T04:49:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T04:49:57Z","body":"Good question 😅\nI think I will need to check the physical structure of the accelerometer and how it works to answer it properly.\nBut from the data we have maybe we can kinda explain it similarly to how a stretchy string with a weight works when you move it quickly.\nLet's say you have a string that can stretch (or a spring), you hold one end of it and on the other end a weight is connected.\nWhen you hold it still, it points to the ground and it has some default length as expected (similarly to when the Z value is -9.8). When you quickly move it down, the weight will move closer to the hand at first (similarly to you getting -5), but after you stop moving the weight will quickly fall down, causing the string/spring to stretch (similarly to you getting -16).\nI hope it makes sense :D","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788218164/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3789931947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3789931947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3789931947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7h5cWr","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T12:03:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:03:26Z","body":"Sure, I will add a reference to the Android documentation later when I can!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3789931947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3913153034","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3913153034","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":3913153034,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pPfoK","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T08:51:58Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T09:05:10Z","body":"As mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/11692#discussion_r2815386332, here is the phone diagram I made, on the same principle as the controller. Feel free to use it if it helps!\r\n![accelerometer_phone](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/828fd8e8-aac6-4149-9e3e-42e09ea7c021)\r\n\r\nI took this opportunity to skim through the discussion above about the values being reported, and will add my own interpretation, without having tested it with my own phone:\r\n\r\nEach accelerometer (X, Y, Z) behaves like a small mass attached to a spring and constrained to move only along its own axis (this is technically not true, as it would introduce oscillations, but we'll ignore that part or assume perfect damping). With the phone lying face up on a table, X is at the center, and reports zero. If you move the phone to the right, the accelerometer will, from inertia, lag behind and report a negative value; if you keep moving the phone at a constant velocity to the right, acceleration of course goes back to zero because of the spring. When you stop moving the phone, inertia keeps the mass moving until the spring brings it back, and you get a positive reading.\r\n\r\nNow for the Z axis, with the phone still lying face up: gravity pulls the accelerometer's mass towards the ground, which is the -Z direction, so you get a -9.8 reading. If you lift the phone, the mass gets pulled further, and you get -10, -11, or lower values. The same of course applies for +Z and the Y axis.\r\n\r\nIn other words, the accelerometer reports the same values you would as a human passenger inside a moving car :smile: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3913153034/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4496340627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-4496340627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":4496340627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDAC2kw","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T08:41:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T08:41:43Z","body":"Now that I think about it, maybe it would be better to create a mobile sensors tutorial in the documentation, that way we can have more text that would explain how the sensors and the methods work, and we will have enough space to put the mobile phone diagram by Cykyrios. We can then link this tutorial from the methods' class reference.\r\nI will work on this later when I can.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4496340627/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4497980011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-4497980011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","id":4497980011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDBm6aw","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T11:38:34Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T11:42:32Z","body":"@Cykyrios Hello, may I ask if a phone diagram similar to the one above but with the phone being horizontal can also be created to show the axis directions in landscape mode, if that's okay and if that's easy to do, please? The methods use Y up/down regardless of the orientation (so, for example, `Input.get_gravity().y` should be about `-9.8` while the phone is at rest in any orientation (portrait, landscape, reverse portrait, and reverse landscape), based on my testing, and the results are similar for other axes), so I think it would be better to show that in the documentation too, in a way that would be easy to understand.\r\nSee also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-3763093823\r\n> And I also should specify where the \"up\" is depending on the phone's orientation (portrait or landscape)\r\n\"Note that the up vector (up direction) always points to the upper side of the phone's screen that is natural to the current orientation (portrait or landscape).\" if that makes sense","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4497980011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4498710250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113635#issuecomment-4498710250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113635","i